Z||000000||gangrenefiero||10-10-2001||01:41 PM||||A big thing now is those indiglo gauges. I like the way they look plus you can get them in green  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So i was wondering if anyone out there knows if you can just get like a sheet of it and if it can be cut. If i could get that it would be cool. I know they make neon in cutable sheets but its like 100 + dollars for a small piece. But if someone knows anything about it let me know. Thanks <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/uforiagman/pic/greenfierorealthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||10-10-2001||01:45 PM||||Contact your local 3M dealer.<P>It's called Durel.<P>Fiero's tend to eat the power inverters needed tfor the EL sheet. I don't know if it's my car or what it is . But I have popped 3 inverters. Some sort of power surge when the lights are turned on.<P>Easy to work with , take your time.<P>JM ||||reg||1
